# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx` and `src/components/bottom-nav.module.css`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages. Do not wrap it in `<main>`, flex shells, or page layouts.

- Do NOT `position: fixed` on `html`. Do NOT make `body` a flex column.
- Nav geometry lives in `bottom-nav.module.css` (`.fixedNav` / `.navInner`): `position: fixed; bottom: 0; height: 50px`. Do not restyle it with Tailwind position/height/padding utilities.
- Do NOT add `pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]`, `pb-safe`, or `mb-safe` on the nav or its inner wrappers.
- Do NOT hide the nav on route change.

Every route uses `PageShell` with `w-full min-h-full pb-[70px] pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)] bg-background`.
Do not add a second `pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]` on pages.
`PageHeader` is not sticky.
